cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "IC Trainer: an interactive app to learn EEG independent component classification"
abstract: >-
  IC Trainer is an interactive web app that trains people to classify EEG
  independent components (neural, blink, eye movement, muscle, bad channel,
  rare event, mixed/other) before removing artifacts, following the practical
  guide by Chaumon, Bishop and Busch (2015). It combines a learning section,
  single-component practice with feedback, and full-dataset review scored with
  signal detection measures against SASICA-style automated measures. All
  components are simulated for teaching.
  Developed during the personal projects session (hackathon) of the
  Training School of Working Group 3 of the INDoS COST Action (CA24161),
  Madrid, 30 September to 2 October 2026.
